Read AGENTS.md first. Summary of what must not change without an ADR:

- React Router v8 **framework mode** only. No Next.js, Astro, declarative mode
  or data mode.
- `ssr: false` is intentional. There is no production frontend Node runtime.
- Public SEO routes are pre-rendered via the official `prerender` option, listed
  in `app/content/prerender-paths.ts`. A `loader` on any other route is a bug.
- Runtime routes (`/hv`, `/hlv`, `/studio`) are served by the SPA fallback at
  `build/client/__spa-fallback.html` and must survive a hard refresh.
- The backend is authoritative. Route guards and hidden buttons are UX, never
  authorization.
- No frontend BFF, no custom SSR, no Server Actions, no RSC.
- New architecture requires an ADR in `docs/adr/`.

Run `npm run verify` before claiming anything is done.
